# Architecture

Use a modular monolith with ports-and-adapters. No DI container, no service locator, no new god `*Manager`.

1. Dependencies point inward. Domain must not import adapters, presentation, Google SDKs, TUI, filesystem libraries, or process libraries.
2. Constructor injection. One composition root per process (`bootstrap/daemon.ts`, `bootstrap/client.ts`).
3. Ports exist only at replaceable boundaries (`ProcessRuntime`, `Clock`, `FileSystem`, `CredentialProvider`). Do not invent `IService` / `IServiceManager`.
4. CLI, TUI, and MCP share application commands. Presentation must not start or kill processes.
5. Commands are explicit calls. Events are facts that already happened. Do not hide control flow on the event bus.
6. Separate `ServiceDefinition` (config) from `ServiceRuntime` (live state). Config becomes an immutable snapshot after load.
7. Google Cloud stays an adapter. Local-only services must run without it.
8. Split decisions into policies/resolvers. Use an explicit lifecycle state machine for service transitions.
9. Keep module public APIs small. `bun run check:architecture` must stay green.

```ts
// BAD — domain reaches Google
import { GoogleAuth } from "google-auth-library";

// GOOD — application depends on a port
constructor(private readonly credentials: CredentialProvider) {}
```
